<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of White Mountain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1620">1620</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of White Mountain was fought near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> on 8 November 1620, early in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. Imperial and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> troops defeated the army of the Bohemian Estates and their elected king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-v-of-the-palatinate">Frederick V of the Palatinate</a>. The defeat led to the re-Catholicisation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, the loss of the Palatine electorate to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> absolutism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-white-mountain.jpg" alt="Battle of White Mountain" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Snayers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_White_Mountain_(by_Peter_Snayers).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Maximilian I built a disciplined standing force, founded the Catholic League in 1609 and, with its general Count Tilly, shared in the Catholic victory at the <b>Battle of White Mountain</b> near Prague in 1620.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>His army was destroyed at the <b>Battle of White Mountain</b> on 8 November 1620, Spanish troops under Spinola occupied the left bank, and in 1622 the Catholic League's army under Tilly took Heidelberg.</blockquote><a href="/empire/electoral-palatinate">Electoral Palatinate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Thirty Years’ War the Bohemian revolt was crushed at the <b>Battle of White Mountain</b> on 8 November 1620, and imperial armies raised by Albrecht von Wallenstein fought across Germany until the Peace of Westphalia in 1648.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1620 the army of the rebel Bohemian estates was routed at the <b>Battle of White Mountain</b> outside Prague.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Bohemian estates, which had elected Habsburgs since 1526, deposed the Habsburg Ferdinand in 1619 and elected Frederick V of the Palatinate, the “Winter King”; after the <b>Battle of White Mountain</b> in 1620 the Habsburgs abolished the elective crown.</blockquote><a href="/government/elective-monarchy">Elective monarchy · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>Duke Maximilian I, head of the Catholic League, helped crush the Bohemian revolt at the <b>White Mountain</b> in 1620.</blockquote><a href="/state/electorate-of-bavaria">Electorate of Bavaria</a></li></ul></section>
